{
  "name": "Upload a CSV of email addresses and download it with a check result per address",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Upload a CSV of email addresses and download it with a check result per address\n\n### How it works\nCheck a list before it bounces. The form accepts a CSV file with an email column (other columns are kept as they are). The workflow reads the file, removes duplicate addresses, keeps the first max_rows and checks each one with Argorant. Every row gets status (valid, invalid, catch_all, risky or unknown) and send yes or no, and the form offers the result as a CSV download.\n\nCosts: half a credit per fresh check; recent checks are free.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Set max_rows in **Settings**.\n4. Activate the workflow and share the production URL of **Upload form**.\n\n### Customization\nReturn only the rows with send yes, or email the file to the person who uploaded it.",
        "height": 602,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "772c9a98-f24d-410b-9a85-39adf9751625",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Read the upload\nDuplicates removed, at most max_rows checks per upload.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 940,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "56feb42c-bb1b-4125-987a-04e36dd8f4a6",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
